5. Agent Manager upgrade requirements

The existing Agent Manager must become ecosystem-neutral.

It should support:

- Individual agents
- Agent groups
- Agent bundles
- Agent ecosystems
- Local agents
- Remote agents
- Sub-agents
- Workflow agents
- Coding agents
- External agent harnesses

ECC agents should receive stable HOPE identities that do not depend only on display names.

Each agent must record:

- Stable identity
- Parent ecosystem
- Source identity
- Display name
- Purpose
- Supported tasks
- Input schema
- Output schema
- Required skills
- Required tools
- Required API capabilities
- Required model qualities
- Runtime type
- Workspace permissions
- Network permissions
- Data-access permissions
- Risk level
- Approval requirements
- Resource limits
- Operating-system requirements
- Version
- Source repository
- Source commit
- Source hash
- Health status

Agent Manager must use runtime drivers instead of hardcoded provider integrations.

Supported driver categories should include:

- Python SDK
- Node SDK
- CLI
- Docker
- HTTP
- A2A
- MCP
- Local process
- Remote process
- Ecosystem adapter

Agent Manager must support coordination between:

- HOPE
- ECC planner
- ECC implementation agent
- ECC test agent
- ECC reviewer
- ECC security agent
- Other sub-agents
- External repositories
- API providers

It must preserve task ownership, execution history, approvals, artifacts, logs, and final results.

