6. Agent lifecycle and readiness

Agent Manager must clearly distinguish between different states.

Required states include:

- Discovered
- Imported
- Installed
- Configured
- Loaded
- Ready
- Degraded
- Blocked
- Simulated
- Failed
- Disabled
- Updating
- Rolled back

An agent must not appear fully ready merely because its metadata was imported.

For example, an ECC reviewer may be imported successfully but remain degraded because:

- The repository is not mounted
- Required skills are missing
- The API is unavailable
- The sandbox is blocked
- Git is unavailable
- Required tools are missing
- Permissions have not been approved

The Agent Manager dashboard must show the exact reason for every non-ready state and provide repair or approval actions where possible.

The user must be able to:

- Open a direct agent dashboard
- Start a conversation
- Assign work
- Enable or disable the agent
- Test readiness
- View permissions
- View tools
- View skills
- View API/model selection
- View runtime
- View logs
- Retry a failed task
- Repair the agent
- Roll back an update
- Remove the agent

Double-clicking an agent must open an actionable dashboard, not a static information page.

Right-click actions should include:

- Chat
- Assign task
- Test
- Enable
- Disable
- Repair
- Update
- View permissions
- View context
- View activity
- View logs
- Remove

