13. Security Manager requirements

ECC must be treated as untrusted external software until reviewed.

Security Manager should scan:

- Repository source
- Installation scripts
- Hooks
- Shell scripts
- MCP configurations
- Agent instructions
- Prompt-injection content
- Dependencies
- Secrets
- Network access
- File operations
- Runtime scripts
- Configuration files

Security Manager must produce:

- Findings
- Severity
- Affected component
- Recommended action
- Whether execution is blocked
- Whether user approval is sufficient
- Whether the component should be disabled

Security review must be attached to the ecosystem and to individual components.

The user must be able to disable a dangerous hook or skill without removing the complete ECC ecosystem.

Every security decision must be recorded in the audit trail.

