The user must be able to work with ECC through HOPE’s normal conversation system.

Supported interaction modes:

- Ask HOPE to use ECC automatically
- Select ECC directly
- Select a specific ECC agent
- Chat with the planner
- Chat with the implementation agent
- Chat with the reviewer
- Chat with the security agent
- Assign a repository task
- Approve a plan
- Approve file changes
- Approve shell commands
- Review test results
- Review security findings
- Review the final diff
- Continue interrupted work

The interface must show live statuses such as:

- Thinking
- Planning
- Working
- Reading
- Editing
- Running tests
- Reviewing
- Generating
- Coding
- Surfacing
- Collecting
- Waiting for approval
- Blocked
- Completed
- Failed

The user must not have to guess whether an agent is working or silently stuck.

Each task should have:

